deepin-liferaft (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Restyle the dialog in native Deepin style: a rounded alert banner with the
    warning badge, a DListView with the alternating row shading of Deepin
    System Monitor, and a separator above right-aligned Resume and Force Quit
    buttons, all following the DTK palette and light/dark theme.
  * Label the application list columns with Application and Memory.
  * Show the machine's total and available memory and its swap under the alert,
    refreshed with every poll and taken from the same /proc/meminfo sample as
    the pressure decision.
  * Ask for confirmation before closing the window while applications are still
    paused, so a stray close cannot silently resume them; SIGTERM and SIGINT
    still thaw without asking.

 -- Ston Jia <ston.jia@outlook.com>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:02:27 +0800

deepin-liferaft (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Install /etc/default/grub.d/90_deepin_liferaft.cfg to enable kernel PSI
    (psi=1) idempotently, and run update-grub in postinst so memory.pressure
    is available on CONFIG_PSI_DEFAULT_DISABLED=y kernels after the next boot.
  * Document PSI auto-enable and the already-present global enable of the user
    service for all graphical-session users in README and the manual page.

 -- Ston Jia <ston.jia@outlook.com>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 13:10:19 +0800

